  <prompt>
    Serialize the barrel work Group A was barred from: export the three new renderers (DateField,
    NumberField, BooleanField) from fields/index.ts and components/RecordHeader/index.ts. Then write the
    shared renderer-CONTRACT test suite asserting that every renderer obeys FR-10 identically — props
    shape, self-applied gridColumn, editable gate, draft/commit/revert-on-reject-stay-in-edit,
    Enter/Escape, blur-commits, em-dash for null/undefined/'' — with per-renderer interaction adapters.
    Where a renderer violates the contract, fix the renderer here (serially — no race) and document the
    fix; where the violation is a contract question, escalate.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in React Testing Library, parameterized test design, and the
    Fluent v9 / React 16-17 shared-library boundary. Follow ADRs strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Both barrels export all renderers + prop types; a NEW parameterized suite
    __tests__/rendererContract.test.tsx passes against all six field renderers (TextField, TextareaField,
    OptionSetField, DateField, NumberField, BooleanField); the full shared-library test suite and build
    are green; any conformance fixes made to renderer files are documented in
    projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/renderer-contract-reconciliation.md.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-10 acceptance is literally "contract test suite passes identically against every renderer" —
      this task IS that acceptance. It exists as a separate serial task because R1 lost time to parallel
      renderer tasks racing on fields/index.ts (plan.md Strategy point 3: "The barrel serializes");
      tasks 010-014 each carried a MUST-NOT-edit-the-barrel constraint pointing here. The
      fields/index.ts header comment documents the one-line-per-renderer append convention;
      components/RecordHeader/index.ts (lines 19-34) documents the explicit-named re-export convention
      (NO `export *` — it exists to dodge a LookupField name collision).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/fields/index.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/index.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/__tests__/rendererContract.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/fields/TextField.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/__tests__/fields.test.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">DateField.tsx + its unit tests</dependency>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">NumberField.tsx + its unit tests</dependency>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">BooleanField.tsx + its unit tests</dependency>
      <dependency task="013" status="pending">OptionSetField edit mode + typography fix</dependency>
      <dependency task="014" status="pending">TextField em-dash '' alignment</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Barrel scope: APPEND-only, following each barrel's documented convention — one export line + one type line per renderer in fields/index.ts; explicit-named re-exports (never `export *`) in components/RecordHeader/index.ts. Do not reorder or restructure existing export lines.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">NFR-08 / DEF-06 (scope: both barrel files and package.json): do NOT add an `exports` map to package.json, do NOT change moduleResolution, do NOT "clean up" anything about how consumers deep-path import from dist/* — the deep paths are load-bearing for PCF bundle size and the exports migration is explicitly out of R2 scope.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">The contract suite tests a pure rendering contract through the public props — no mocking of renderer internals, no DI-registration-style tests, no snapshot-only assertions. This is a KEEP-category suite (it guards a cross-component contract that outlives the project).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">The test file and any conformance fixes stay React 16/17-safe; conformance fixes to renderer files stay semantic-tokens-only (ADR-021).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Contract-violation handling (scope: any renderer failing the suite): FIX the renderer in this task with the minimal conformance change and record it in notes/renderer-contract-reconciliation.md (what, why, which suite assertion caught it). If the fix would change shipped public behavior a consumer depends on (e.g. TextareaField's commit key), that is the escalation trigger — do not weaken the suite and do not fork the contract.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Documented per-renderer allowances (the ONLY permitted deviations, encoded as suite parameters, not skipped tests): TextareaField's commit key is its documented Ctrl/Cmd+Enter (plain Enter inserts a newline — shipped R1 behavior); OptionSetField's commit gesture is option-selection in the Dropdown; DateField/NumberField/BooleanField per their task specs. The display-only RecordHeader LookupField is OUT of this suite's scope (different value-shape props, no onSave) — note this exclusion in the suite header comment.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Renderer contract testing; barrel export conventions; test architecture</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
