    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="contract source of truth" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/fields/TextField.tsx">FR-10 is defined as "the TextField contract verbatim" — every suite assertion derives from observable TextField behavior: editable gate (:118), revert-on-reject-stay-in-edit (:150-153), Enter/Escape (:165-176), blur-commit (:206), spinner (:212), self-applied span (:181).</pattern>
      <pattern name="existing test harness" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/__tests__/fields.test.tsx">Use the same `renderWithProviders` from `../../../__mocks__/pcfMocks` and the same span-assertion technique (inline style gridColumn). Do NOT modify this file — the contract suite is a NEW sibling, and the per-renderer describe blocks in fields.test.tsx remain as-is.</pattern>
      <pattern name="barrel conventions" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/index.ts">Lines 19-34 document WHY explicit-named re-exports are used (LookupField collision). Follow it; extend the comment only if you add a colliding name (you should not).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Context + rigor declaration per task-execute Step 0.5. Read all six renderer files as they now exist post-Group-A, plus both barrels and fields.test.tsx.</step>
    <step order="1">Update fields/index.ts: append export + type lines for BooleanField/IBooleanFieldProps, DateField/IDateFieldProps, NumberField/INumberFieldProps (alphabetical placement consistent with the file's existing order; one line per renderer per its header comment).</step>
    <step order="2">Update components/RecordHeader/index.ts: add explicit-named re-exports for the three new renderers + prop types, following the documented convention. Verify no name collides with an existing top-level component export (grep the top-level src/index.ts surface for DateField/NumberField/BooleanField before choosing un-aliased names; alias like RecordHeaderLookupField only if a collision actually exists).</step>
    <step order="3">Design the contract suite: a parameterized harness (e.g. an array of per-renderer adapter objects driving shared `describe.each` blocks) where each adapter supplies: component, minimal props factory, a sample non-empty value + its expected rendered text, an empty-value triple (null/undefined/''), an edit-entry gesture, a draft-change gesture, the commit gesture (per the documented allowances), and the expected onSave payload. Cover all six renderers: TextField, TextareaField, OptionSetField, DateField, NumberField, BooleanField.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the shared assertions for EVERY renderer: (a) label + value render; (b) `gridColumn: span N` self-applied for spans 1/2/3; (c) null, undefined, and '' each render `—`; (d) no onSave = no editable affordance; (e) onSave + disabled=true = not editable; (f) commit gesture calls onSave exactly once with the adapter's expected payload and exits edit on resolve; (g) Escape cancels with zero onSave calls; (h) blur commits a changed draft; (i) rejected onSave reverts the draft AND stays in edit mode with a spinner during the pending save; (j) required=true renders the `*` marker ONLY for TextField — the other five render NO marker (D-10 negative assertion).</step>
    <step order="5">Run the suite. For each failure, decide: renderer bug → minimal conformance fix in the renderer file + entry in notes/renderer-contract-reconciliation.md; contract question → escalation trigger. Iterate until green with zero skipped tests.</step>
    <step order="6">Run the FULL shared-library suite (`npm test`) and `npm run build` in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components; both must exit 0. Verify fields.test.tsx is untouched in git diff.</step>
    <step order="7">Write notes/renderer-contract-reconciliation.md (even if empty of fixes — record "no violations found" explicitly, listing the six renderers verified).</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">If any deviations from plan occurred, document in projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If bringing a renderer into conformance requires changing shipped public behavior that an existing consumer depends on (e.g. TextareaField's Ctrl/Cmd+Enter commit key, or any behavior MatterHeaderPcf v1.0.20 renders today), STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6 — renegotiating the FR-10 contract or grandfathering a deviation is the operator's call, not the suite author's.</trigger>
    <trigger>If two Group-A outputs landed mutually inconsistent interpretations of the contract (e.g. different rejected-save semantics) such that no single suite can pass both without one being rewritten, STOP and escalate with the diff evidence rather than silently rewriting one renderer's semantics.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Mixed-grid renderer parity (visual)">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_invoice&amp;id={record-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Open a bound header showing text, date, number, optionset, and boolean cells in one grid (executes at Phase 5 tasks 050/051/060/061)</step>
        <step>Verify every label has identical typography (size, weight, color) and every empty value shows `—`</step>
        <step>Enter and cancel edit on one cell of each type; verify identical interaction feel (click-to-edit, Escape cancels)</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Six renderers indistinguishable in chrome and interaction except for their value-type-specific editors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle dark mode in the app</step>
        <step>Verify a mixed grid of all renderer types adapts completely — labels, value cells, em-dashes, and open editors (input, picker, dropdown, switch)</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colors resolve from Fluent v9 semantic tokens per ADR-021; no renderer stands out in dark mode</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build + test the shared library</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">git diff verification; grep for export-collision check</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
