  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`import { DateField, NumberField, BooleanField } from './fields'` type-checks from components/RecordHeader/index.ts, and all three (plus their prop types) are re-exported from the RecordHeader barrel with no `export *` introduced.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The contract suite runs its shared assertion set against ALL SIX renderers (TextField, TextareaField, OptionSetField, DateField, NumberField, BooleanField) — six adapter entries exist and none is skipped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">For every renderer: null, undefined, and '' each render `—`; `gridColumn: span N` is self-applied for spans 1, 2, and 3; no onSave = read-only; onSave + disabled=true = read-only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">For every renderer: the commit gesture calls onSave exactly once with the adapter's expected payload; Escape exits edit with zero onSave calls; blur commits a changed draft.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative, for every renderer: a rejected onSave reverts the draft to the prior value AND leaves the component IN edit mode, with the spinner shown while the rejection is pending.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (D-10): with required=true, the `*` marker renders for TextField and for NO other renderer — asserted for all six.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">__tests__/fields.test.tsx is untouched in git diff; every pre-existing test still passes; the FULL `npm test` and `npm run build` in Spaarke.UI.Components exit 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/renderer-contract-reconciliation.md exists and either lists each conformance fix (file, behavior, catching assertion) or states "no violations found" over the six verified renderers.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (NFR-08): package.json gained no `exports` map and no consumer-facing import path changed — `git diff` on package.json is empty.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <completion-notes date="2026-08-25">
